    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>One of the five <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan-sultanates">Deccan sultanates</a> that replaced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a>, ruled by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adil-shahi-dynasty">Adil Shahi dynasty</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bijapur">Bijapur</a>.</li><li>It joined the coalition that defeated Vijayanagara at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-talikota">Talikota</a> in 1565 and later conquered much of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>.</li><li>Squeezed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> and the rising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a>, it fell to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a> after a long siege in 1686.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gol-gumbaz">Gol Gumbaz</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bijapur">Bijapur</a>, tomb of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-adil-shah">Muhammad Adil Shah</a>, has a whispering gallery under its dome where a whisper can be heard clearly on the far side.</p></aside>
    </section>

